# API routes (`web/app/api/**)

Open [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) only when changing caching strategy or deal-engine wiring.

## Expensive or abuse-prone routes

Use `lib/rateLimit.ts` (`checkRateLimit`, `clientIp`, `rateLimitResponse`):

| Route | Suggested limit |
|-------|-----------------|
| `POST analyze-url` | 10 / 15 min / IP |
| `POST subscribe` | 5 / hour / IP |
| `POST reports/share` | 20 / hour / IP |
| `GET nearby-amenities` | 30 / min / IP |

Wire new expensive endpoints the same way.

`lib/rateLimit.ts` is **process-local memory**. Limits do not share across instances and reset on restart — fine for single-node; use Redis/Upstash before multi-instance prod (see roadmap).

## Read paths

- Hot reads: wrap with `lib/serverCache.ts` + `Cache-Control: s-maxage`.
- Parse inputs manually; bound numerics (prices, coords, page sizes). No Zod yet — validate explicitly.
- Errors: `try/catch` → `NextResponse.json({ error: "..." }, { status })` + `console.error`.
- Nearby amenities: Overpass failures return `{ unavailable: true }` (200); do not cache unavailable payloads.

## Security

- SQL: Prisma or `Prisma.sql` with parameters only.
- External fetch: host allowlists only. Analyze-url → `fincaraiz.com.co` **and** `metrocuadrado.com` (`lib/analyzeListingUrl.ts`).
- Email HTML: escape user/scraped strings via `lib/htmlEscape.ts`.
- Cron: `CRON_SECRET` Bearer (or `?secret=`); deny in prod if unset. Ops: `docs/EMAIL_OPERATIONS.md`.
- Do not log secrets or full tokens.

## Deal data

Scoring logic lives in `lib/dealEngine.ts` — change it only with scraper parity in mind. Live analysis entry (shared pool + house floor): `lib/dealCompPool.ts` → `analyzeListingDeal`. Opportunities hot path: `lib/getTopOpportunities.ts`. Listing detail / analyze-url: `lib/getListingDetail.ts`.
